# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TokenTicks environment
#
# Every variable here is PUBLIC. Vite inlines anything prefixed VITE_ into the
# browser bundle, so nothing secret belongs in this file. Secrets (the Supabase
# service-role key, the Lemon Squeezy webhook signing secret) are set on the
# Supabase Edge Function, never here.
#
# All of it is optional. With none of it set, the app runs as a fully working
# local token counter and cost dashboard: accounts and paid features report as
# unavailable rather than breaking.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Project settings -> API. Use the anon / publishable key, NOT service_role;
# the app refuses to start with a service_role key here and explains why.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Lemon Squeezy ----------------------------------------------------------
# The checkout base for your store, without a trailing variant id.
VITE_LEMON_CHECKOUT_URL=https://your-store.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy

# Variant UUIDs - the last path segment of each variant's "Copy checkout URL",
# e.g. 9d4e1f2a-7c3b-4e5d-8a9f-1b2c3d4e5f60. NOT the numeric variant_id: that
# one belongs in the Edge Function secrets below, and a number here produces a
# 404 on the checkout link. The Pro annual one is optional; without it the
# annual toggle falls back to monthly for that plan.
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_PRO_MONTHLY=
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_PRO_ANNUAL=
VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_TEAM_MONTHLY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set on the Edge Function only — `supabase secrets set KEY=value`, or
# Supabase -> Edge Functions -> Secrets:
#
#   LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET   signing secret from the webhook settings
#   LEMON_PRO_VARIANT_IDS          comma-separated numeric ids of the Pro
#                                  variants
#   LEMON_TEAM_VARIANT_IDS         the same for Team
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY      injected by the platform; do not set by hand
#
# Both variant lists are required and a purchase of anything in neither is
# refused with a 500 that names the id. The webhook used to default an
# unrecognised variant to Pro, which meant a $39 Team subscription quietly
# bought $12 of product.
#
# Note these are NOT the same values as the VITE_LEMON_VARIANT_* above: a
# checkout link is built from the variant's UUID, while a webhook reports
# attributes.variant_id as a number. `node scripts/billing-preflight.mjs` says
# which half is configured.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
